# Make It Work First / Làm cho chạy trước

Default workflow for **every new request or function** in this frontend repo.

## Phase 1: Make it work (default)

**Mục tiêu:** Code chạy được, logic đúng, end-to-end.

- Implement the smallest change that satisfies the request
- Wire API, state, routing, and UI enough to verify behavior
- Match existing project patterns; don't invent new architecture
- Skip polish: no premature refactor, DRY sweeps, or "perfect" UI
- Do **not** touch unrelated files or refactor code outside the task scope
- Verify it runs (build, manual flow, or stated acceptance path)

**Example — new feature:** User asks for "export list filter by date"
→ Add filter state, call existing service with params, show filtered results. Done when filter works.

**Example — bug fix:** Fix the broken path only. No drive-by cleanup.

## Phase 2: Make it right (explicit user request only)

**Chỉ khi user yêu cầu rõ:** "Make it right", refactor, clean code, maintainability, extensibility.

Then you may:
- Extract components/hooks, improve naming, tighten types
- DRY duplicated logic, simplify structure
- Add tests when they add real value
- Polish UI/UX if requested

**Example:** After export filter works, user says "Make it right"
→ Extract `useExportDateFilter`, shared filter UI, stronger types, clearer file layout.

## Do NOT

- Start new work with ideal architecture or full abstractions
- Refactor unrelated code during Phase 1
- Enter Phase 2 without an explicit user ask

When unsure which phase applies: **default to Phase 1**.
